   "midterm": "7–15",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers firefighter health and wellness, physical fitness, injury prevention, scene safety, accountability, incident safety responsibilities, and accident and near-miss investigations.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Firefighting requires physical and mental readiness.\n- Accidents, injuries, and near misses should be investigated.\n- Firefighters must recognize and report unsafe practices.\n- Personnel accountability systems track members, assignments, and activities.\n- Firefighters should maintain crew integrity.\n- Hydroplaning occurs when water separates tires from the road surface.\n- Apparatus should stage away from violent scenes until law enforcement declares them safe.\n- Safety officers monitor incident hazards and unsafe operations.\n\n### Important References\n\n- NFPA 1851: Protective ensemble care and maintenance, as named in the exam.\n- NFPA 1010: Firefighter professional qualifications.\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **NFPA 1851** — Protective ensemble care and maintenance, as named in the exam.\n- **NFPA 1010** — Firefighter professional qualifications.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nFirefighter safety requires fitness, risk awareness, accountability, safe operations, and reporting of unsafe conditions.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 2\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
