   "midterm": "16–24",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers structural firefighting PPE, protective coats, pants, helmets, gloves, boots, and hoods, SCBA components, respiratory protection, PPE inspection, cleaning, and maintenance, and air management.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- PPE reduces exposure to hazards but does not eliminate risk.\n- SCBA supplies breathable air independently of the surrounding atmosphere.\n- SCBA harness: Frame and straps securing the apparatus.\n- Closed-circuit SCBA: Rebreather.\n- Supplied-air respirator: Receives air from a remote source.\n- PASS: Personal Alert Safety System.\n- Protective hoods protect the head and neck.\n- Clean and inspect PPE according to manufacturer and department instructions.\n- Skip breathing is a breathing technique described in the chapter; it does not replace safe air management.\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **SCBA harness** — Frame and straps securing the apparatus.\n- **Closed-circuit SCBA** — Rebreather.\n- **Supplied-air respirator** — Receives air from a remote source.\n- **PASS** — Personal Alert Safety System.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nKnow PPE components, respiratory protection differences, SCBA operation, and equipment limitations.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 3\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
