   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers fire dispatch, radio communications, emergency communications, Mayday procedures, LUNAR, communications centers, and telephone and digital communications.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Dispatch: Select, alert, and communicate with responding units.\n- FCC: Federal Communications Commission.\n- Simplex: Radio communication in one direction at a time.\n- ANI: Automatic Number Identification.\n- VoIP: Voice over Internet Protocol.\n- Time marks: Periodic incident-time notifications.\n- Mayday: Emergency request for firefighter assistance.\n- Evacuation signal: Warns firefighters to withdraw.\n\n### LUNAR\n\n- L: Location\n- U: Unit\n- N: Name\n- A: Air supply or Assignment\n- R: Resources needed\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **Dispatch** — Select, alert, and communicate with responding units.\n- **FCC** — Federal Communications Commission.\n- **Simplex** — Radio communication in one direction at a time.\n- **ANI** — Automatic Number Identification.\n- **VoIP** — Voice over Internet Protocol.\n- **Time marks** — Periodic incident-time notifications.\n- **Mayday** — Emergency request for firefighter assistance.\n- **Evacuation signal** — Warns firefighters to withdraw.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nKnow LUNAR, dispatch terminology, radio basics, and emergency communications.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 4\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
