   "midterm": "43, 46–51, 140",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers structural systems, building materials, roof construction, building construction types, structural loads, fire resistance, and collapse hazards.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Heat reduces the strength of structural materials.\n- Gravity acts on structural members and can contribute to collapse.\n- According to the supplied chapter, steel loses approximately half its strength at 650°F.\n- Heavy timber construction uses large wooden posts and beams.\n- Rafter: Inclined structural roof member.\n- Flat roofs have a slight slope for drainage.\n- Cape Cod houses often contain knee walls and concealed spaces.\n- Lightweight structural assemblies can present significant collapse hazards.\n- Firefighters must continually evaluate structural conditions.\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **Rafter** — Inclined structural roof member.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nKnow how buildings are constructed and how structural components respond to fire.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 6\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
