   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers hand tools, cutting tools, power tools, equipment inspection, tool maintenance, tool selection, and safe tool operation.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n### Important Tools\n\n- Ventilation saw: Creates roof ventilation openings.\n- Diagonal cutter: Cuts wire and small cable.\n- Rabbit tool: Hydraulic forcible-entry spreading tool.\n- Closet hook: Short hook used in tight spaces.\n- Hacksaw: Saw with blade in a U-shaped frame.\n- Cutting torch: Cutting tool that presents ignition hazards.\n- Halligan: Multipurpose forcible-entry tool.\n- Flathead axe: Cutting and striking tool.\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **Ventilation saw** — Creates roof ventilation openings.\n- **Diagonal cutter** — Cuts wire and small cable.\n- **Rabbit tool** — Hydraulic forcible-entry spreading tool.\n- **Closet hook** — Short hook used in tight spaces.\n- **Hacksaw** — Saw with blade in a U-shaped frame.\n- **Cutting torch** — Cutting tool that presents ignition hazards.\n- **Halligan** — Multipurpose forcible-entry tool.\n- **Flathead axe** — Cutting and striking tool.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nIdentify tools, understand their uses, and recognize operational hazards.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 7\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
