   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter will cover fire extinguisher classifications, extinguishing agents, extinguisher components, extinguisher selection, appropriate extinguisher applications, and inspection and safe use. Full chapter review remains pending.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n### Starter Facts from the Midterm\n\n- Class A: Ordinary combustibles.\n- Class B: Flammable liquids and gases.\n- Class C: Energized electrical equipment.\n- Class D: Combustible metals.\n- Class K: Cooking oils and fats.\n- Class K extinguishers are commonly used in commercial kitchens.\n- Sodium bicarbonate is an original dry-chemical extinguishing agent.\n- Water mist extinguishers are typically white.\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **Class A** — Ordinary combustibles.\n- **Class B** — Flammable liquids and gases.\n- **Class C** — Energized electrical equipment.\n- **Class D** — Combustible metals.\n- **Class K** — Cooking oils and fats.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Hartford County Regional Fire School Firefighter I Midterm, questions 70–78\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
