   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter will cover municipal water supply systems, fire hydrants, water distribution, hydrant operation, portable water tanks, and water pressure and flow. Full chapter review remains pending.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n### Starter Facts from the Midterm\n\nMunicipal water systems include:\n\n1. Water source\n2. Water treatment facility\n3. Distribution system\n\n### Additional terms\n\n- Grid arrangement: Water can reach an area through multiple paths.\n- Hydrant barrel: Upright hydrant body.\n- Dry-barrel hydrant: Drains to reduce freezing risk.\n- Friction loss: Loss of pressure caused by water movement resistance.\n\n### Hydrant Color Classifications\n\n- Red: Less than 500 GPM.\n- Orange: 500–999 GPM.\n- Green: 1,000–1,499 GPM.\n- Blue: 1,500 GPM or more\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **Grid arrangement** — Water can reach an area through multiple paths.\n- **Hydrant barrel** — Upright hydrant body.\n- **Dry-barrel hydrant** — Drains to reduce freezing risk.\n- **Friction loss** — Loss of pressure caused by water movement resistance.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Hartford County Regional Fire School Firefighter I Midterm, questions 79–86\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
