   "title": "Fire Hose, Appliances, and Nozzles",
   "midterm": "87–96",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers fire hose construction, attack and supply hose, hose couplings, nozzles, hose appliances, hose maintenance, and hose damage.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Attack hose: Delivers pressurized water onto a fire.\n- Supply hose: Carries water toward a pumper or other supply point.\n- Collapsible hose: Lays flat when unpressurized.\n- Swivel gasket: Seals a threaded hose connection.\n- Shut-off valve: Controls flow at a nozzle.\n- Hose roller: Protects hose moving over edges.\n- Mechanical damage: Includes abrasive damage caused by grit.\n- Bresnan distributor: Device used to apply water into difficult-to-access spaces.\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **Attack hose** — Delivers pressurized water onto a fire.\n- **Supply hose** — Carries water toward a pumper or other supply point.\n- **Collapsible hose** — Lays flat when unpressurized.\n- **Swivel gasket** — Seals a threaded hose connection.\n- **Shut-off valve** — Controls flow at a nozzle.\n- **Hose roller** — Protects hose moving over edges.\n- **Mechanical damage** — Includes abrasive damage caused by grit.\n- **Bresnan distributor** — Device used to apply water into difficult-to-access spaces.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nUnderstand the differences between hose types, couplings, appliances, and nozzles.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 11\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
