   "title": "Supply Line and Attack Line Evolutions",
   "midterm": "97–105",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers hose deployment, hose loading, forward hose lays, reverse hose lays, attack line advancement, and water supply operations.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Flake out: Arrange hose for easy advancement.\n- Forward lay: Water source toward the fire.\n- Reverse lay: Fire toward the water source.\n- Minuteman hose load: Allows a firefighter to release hose folds while advancing.\n- Gated wye: Splits flow into separately controlled outlets.\n- FDC: Fire Department Connection.\n\n### Common Supply Hose Loads\n\n1. Flat load\n2. Horseshoe load\n3. Accordion load\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **Flake out** — Arrange hose for easy advancement.\n- **Forward lay** — Water source toward the fire.\n- **Reverse lay** — Fire toward the water source.\n- **Minuteman hose load** — Allows a firefighter to release hose folds while advancing.\n- **Gated wye** — Splits flow into separately controlled outlets.\n- **FDC** — Fire Department Connection.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nKnow hose loads, forward versus reverse lays, and deployment methods.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 13\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
