   "midterm": "133–141",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers firefighter emergencies, Mayday procedures, lost and trapped firefighters, escape techniques, rapid intervention, downed-firefighter rescue, and breathing-air emergencies.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- LUNAR: Location, Unit, Name, Air/Assignment, Resources.\n- RIC: Rapid Intervention Crew/Company.\n- DRD: Drag Rescue Device.\n- EBSS: Emergency Breathing Safety System.\n- Safe haven: Temporary refuge from danger.\n- Backhanded swim: Escape method for passing through a narrow wall opening.\n- SCBA straps can assist with firefighter removal.\n- Personnel accountability is essential during emergencies.\n\n## Key terms\n\n- **LUNAR** — Location, Unit, Name, Air/Assignment, Resources.\n- **RIC** — Rapid Intervention Crew/Company.\n- **DRD** — Drag Rescue Device.\n- **EBSS** — Emergency Breathing Safety System.\n- **Safe haven** — Temporary refuge from danger.\n- **Backhanded swim** — Escape method for passing through a narrow wall opening.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nRecognize emergencies early, communicate clearly, manage air supply, and maintain escape options.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 19\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
