   "title": "Understanding Fire Investigation",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers the purpose of fire investigation, fire origin and cause, evidence recognition, evidence preservation, chain of custody, and firefighter responsibilities during investigations.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Firefighters may observe conditions that help establish a fire's origin and cause.\n- Preserve the scene when an investigation is required.\n- Avoid unnecessarily disturbing potential evidence.\n- Fire investigators conduct formal investigations.\n- Chain of custody documents evidence handling and transfer.\n- Firefighters should follow investigator and department instructions.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nRecognize and preserve potential fire evidence without compromising scene safety.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 28\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
