   "title": "Recognizing and Identifying the Hazards",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers scene size-up, recognizing hazardous materials, hazardous materials containers, placards and labels, shipping papers, Safety Data Sheets, the Emergency Response Guidebook, and identification numbers.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Approach suspected releases from a safer direction, generally upwind, uphill, and/or upstream.\n- Recognize hazards from a safe distance.\n- Look for placards, labels, container shapes, and visible evidence of a release.\n- UN/NA identification numbers are commonly four digits.\n- Shipping papers help identify hazardous materials being transported.\n- SDS documents provide information about chemical hazards and handling.\n- Use the ERG as an initial transportation incident reference.\n- Do not approach or contact unknown substances without appropriate training and protection.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nRecognize and identify hazards before selecting protective actions.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 30\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
