   "number": 32,
   "title": "Understanding the Hazards",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers hazardous materials containers, bulk and nonbulk packaging, fixed-facility storage, transportation containers, container failures, release hazards, chemical and physical threats, and potential criminal or terrorist use.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Container size, shape, construction, and pressure may provide clues about possible hazards.\n- Pressurized containers may present additional hazards if damaged or heated.\n- A release can create fire, explosion, toxic, corrosive, or environmental hazards.\n- Recognize that secondary hazards may be present.\n- Do not assume a container identifies its contents without reliable supporting information.\n- Use placards, labels, shipping papers, SDS, and other appropriate resources.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nUnderstanding the container and material helps responders anticipate possible consequences.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 32\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
