   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThis chapter covers risk assessment, incident objectives, response planning, protective actions, isolation and evacuation, shelter-in-place, and choosing response strategies.\n\n## Quick notes\n\n- Responder safety is the first priority.\n- Protect threatened people while avoiding unnecessary exposure.\n- Evaluate the material, quantity, conditions, and possible release behavior.\n- Determine whether evacuation or shelter-in-place is appropriate.\n- Follow incident command and department procedures.\n- Response strategies may be offensive, defensive, or non-intervention.\n- Continuously evaluate changing conditions.\n\n## Exam takeaways\n\nDevelop response objectives based on actual conditions, available resources, and responder qualifications.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Firefighter_I_Collected_Chapters.docx, Chapter 33\n- Chapter outline and starter notes supplied by the student's class brief, 2026-11-03.\n"
