   "summary": "The eight-step hazardous materials response process from the combined class handouts.",
   "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
   "body": "\n## Overview\n\nThe combined class handouts include an eight-step response process. These activities may overlap and continue throughout an incident rather than occurring in a strictly linear order.\n\n## The eight steps\n\n1. Site Management and Control\n2. Identifying the Problem\n3. Hazard and Risk Evaluation\n4. Protective Clothing and Equipment\n5. Information Management and Resource Coordination\n6. Implementing Response Objectives\n7. Decontamination\n8. Terminating the Incident\n\n## Still to add\n\n- Create a study page explaining each step.\n- Use short definitions, examples of decision-making considerations, and safety reminders.\n- Clarify that these activities may overlap and continue throughout an incident rather than occurring in a strictly linear order.\n\n## Sources\n\n- HazMat_Combined_Class_Handouts.pdf\n- Class brief 2026-11-03, Part 5 section 4\n"
